Longest Sequence of 1 after flipping a bit

-->Brute Force Approach
package com.basics;

class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] ar = {1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0};

        int max = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < ar.length; i++) {

            int zeroCount = 0;

            for (int j = i; j < ar.length; j++) {

                if (ar[j] == 0) {
                    zeroCount++;
                }

                if (zeroCount > 1) {
                    break;
                }

                int size = j - i + 1;

                if (size > max) {
                    max = size;
                }
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Longest sequence = " + max);
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n²)
Space Complexity: O(1)

-->Optimal:

package com.basics;

class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] ar = {1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0};

        int left = 0;
        int zeroCount = 0;
        int max = 0;

        for (int right = 0; right < ar.length; right++) {

            if (ar[right] == 0) {
                zeroCount++;
            }

            while (zeroCount > 1) {

                if (ar[left] == 0) {
                    zeroCount--;
                }

                left++;
            }

            int size = right - left + 1;

            if (size > max) {
                max = size;
            }
        }

        System.out.println(max);
    }
}


Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)










